 ],
 "method": "Each .mat file converted with battery-data tools/convert_xjtu_mat.py and its cycles computed with tools/cyclers.py (cycle = one charge followed by one discharge; capacity integrated from current) at battery-data 5d881c9, the same values as the cycle_summary rows of the XJTU import. The file's own per-cycle label and reported capacities are carried beside the computed ones. Values are rounded as printed: Ah to 5 decimals, efficiency and volts to 4, seconds to 0.1.",
 "caveats": [
  "Batches 4-6 do not discharge fully: only cycles whose label ends in '[test capacity]' measure capacity; every other discharge figure there is a partial one.",
  "Current sign: charge-positive throughout; recorded as the BDF default because the files carry no capacity column to prove it.",
  "10 cells (2C_battery-2, RW_battery-2 to RW_battery-8, Sim_satellite_battery-2 and -6) have one recording gap over an hour with current flowing after it; it is not integrated into capacity."
 ],
